> **Corollary C (what the count gives for every B; stated at the referee's suggestion).** Let L be the number of live
> levels of the 2-tree of B. The share of 3-good signings of B is at least ρ_2(B) − (L + 1)·W(no 3); more exactly,
> at least ρ_2(B) − (L + 1)·Σ over the live e′ > 1 of 2^(−μ(e′*)). So B has a good signing whenever
> ρ_2(B) > (L + 1)·W(no 3), and the list of what is not proved can be narrowed by the condition
> ρ_2(B) ≤ (L + 1)·0.118569.
> *Proof.* Let ε be 3-bad at 2^j·e″, e″ | n″. By Lemma L3 (a) for q = 2, applied as long as the level of 2 is not
> live, ε is 3-bad at 2^{j′}·e″ with j′ = 0 or j′ a live level of the 2-tree. By Lemma L3 (c) with c = 2^{j′}, ε is
> 3-bad at 2^{j′}, or 3-bad at 2^{j′}·e′ for a live e′ > 1; for each of the L + 1 values of j′ the signings of the
> second kind have share at most Σ over the live e′ of 2^(−μ(e′*)) ≤ W(no 3). ∎
